  <h2>Telehealth consultations</h2>
  <p>Katrina Ridout, Accredited Practising Dietitian, consults by video with clients anywhere in Australia, and in person at Milton Village Medical in Brisbane. Telehealth consultations are held over a secure video link sent to you when you book. You will need a device with a camera and microphone, a stable internet connection and a private space where you can talk freely.</p>
  <p>Telehealth care is the same standard of care as an in-person consultation. If at any point Kat believes a video consultation is not suitable for your needs, she will tell you and suggest an alternative.</p>

  <h2>Bookings and payment</h2>
  <p>Consultations are prepaid at the time of booking. Your booking is confirmed once payment has been received, and you will receive a confirmation email with the video link and any forms to complete beforehand. Current fees are shown on the booking page.</p>
  <p>If you have a GP Chronic Condition Management Plan (GPCCMP) referral or private health extras cover, bring the paperwork to your first consultation. Kat will give you a receipt you can use to claim any rebate you are eligible for. Rebates are paid to you by Medicare or your health fund, not by the practice.</p>

  <h2>Cancellations and rescheduling</h2>
  <p>Please give at least 24 hours' notice if you need to cancel or move your appointment. You can do this using the link in your confirmation email or by emailing <a href="mailto:info@katridout.com.au">info@katridout.com.au</a>. Appointments changed with 24 hours' notice or more can be rescheduled or refunded in full.</p>
  <p>Appointments cancelled or moved with less than 24 hours' notice may be charged the full consultation fee, because the time has been set aside for you and cannot usually be offered to someone else at short notice.</p>

  <h2>Missed appointments</h2>
  <p>If you do not join the video call within 15 minutes of the start time and have not let us know, the appointment is treated as a no-show and the full fee applies. If something unexpected happens, email or call as soon as you can and Kat will do her best to help.</p>
  <p>If Kat is unable to attend for any reason, you will be offered a new time as soon as possible or a full refund.</p>

  <h2>General information and individual advice</h2>
  <p>Content on this website, in guides, emails and social media is general information only. It is not a substitute for individual dietary or medical advice and does not create a practitioner-client relationship.</p>
  <p>Individual advice is given only within a booked consultation, after Kat has taken your history and understood your circumstances. Written plans and resources provided after a consultation are for the named client only.</p>
  <p>Nutrition care works alongside your GP, obstetrician, fertility specialist and other treating practitioners. It does not replace medical care, and you should keep seeing your medical team as they advise.</p>

  <h2>Emergencies</h2>
  <p>Telehealth is not an emergency service. If you or someone else is in immediate danger or needs urgent medical help, call 000 or go to your nearest emergency department. If you are concerned about your health between appointments, contact your GP or maternity care provider.</p>

  <h2>Your records</h2>
  <p>Notes from your consultations, your written plan and any documents you share are kept in secure clinical practice-management software, in line with our <a href="/privacy-policy/">privacy policy</a> and the Australian Privacy Principles. Video consultations are not recorded.</p>
  <p>With your consent, Kat may write to your referring GP or specialist about your care. You can ask for a copy of your records at any time.</p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>Questions about these terms, bookings or your care: <a href="mailto:info@katridout.com.au">info@katridout.com.au</a> or 1300 640 104.</p>
